From 0156fc50ba1851229925f5878a033b4046e6f538 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:57:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 124/128] xwl, icon_manager, wlmeyes: X11 dock-apps as on X11:
 menus, shape, order

- A parent-less override-redirect X11 window (the menu of a dock-app,
  eg. wmcliphist's; a tooltip) is no window anymore: It goes on top of
  everything (the overlay layer), where it placed itself, undecorated. A
  menu holds the pointer as with its X11 grab: A click outside of it goes
  to its client (and to no one else), once, and closes it.
- The shape of a dock-app's icon window (X Shape: wmclock, wmcliphist,
  wmix...) is honored: The tile shows around it, as in Window Maker. The
  surface is clipped to the shape's rectangles (one clipped copy each).
- The icon window is centered again when its size changes (wmcpuload's
  first buffer is smaller).
- Dock-apps meant for the Dock (Dock.Dockapps) go there in that order,
  whichever starts first.
- wlmeyes --dockapp: Only the tile, with the look of wmeyes; the eyes
  follow the pointer over the whole screen (input observation protocol),
  which an X11 wmeyes on XWayland cannot do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
